\cf0 01 / ABOUT\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 A scientist\uc0\u8232 who 
\f4\i teaches.
\f3\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 I am a mathematician and science educator interested in how students learn, experience, and engage with mathematics and physics. My work brings together research, classroom practice, and curriculum development to explore how we can make STEM learning more meaningful, accessible, and intellectually engaging\
\outl0\strokewidth0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After studying mathematics at the Universit\'e0 degli Studi di Torino and education in Germany through Erasmus, I collaborated with the University of Western Australia on the Einstein-First project.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 I have taught mathematics at a professional high school in Italy and now teach mathematics, science, and computer science at a Montessori elementary school in Illinois.\
\outl0\strokewidth0 \
